Setup. 2I as 120 unit quaternions; rotation axes by order, as directions: 12 five-fold, 20 three-fold, 30 two-fold.

T1. Covariance forces E(z) to be diagonal, leaving the N + 1 weights t_m >= 0 free.
   N = 12: diagonal E(z) with random t: covariance defect below 1e-12; a generic pure E(z): defect above 1e-3, so not covariant
   N = 20: diagonal E(z) with random t: covariance defect below 1e-12; a generic pure E(z): defect above 1e-3, so not covariant
   N = 24: diagonal E(z) with random t: covariance defect below 1e-12; a generic pure E(z): defect above 1e-3, so not covariant
   N = 30: diagonal E(z) with random t: covariance defect below 1e-12; a generic pure E(z): defect above 1e-3, so not covariant
   So the admissible transfers are exactly the nonnegative weights (t_-j, ..., t_j): an (N + 1)-parameter cone,
   which normalization (sum of t = 1) cuts to an N-simplex. Positivity, covariance and normalization single out no member.

T2. The barycenter of the simplex and a vertex.
   uniform t, the barycenter (P1, spectral transfer): A_eff over 5 directions spans below 1e-12, and equals Tr A/(N+1) = 23.995675 (below 1e-12)
   vertex t_m = delta_{m,j} (Q-symbol transfer): A_eff over the same 5 directions spans 7.310785
   vertex t_m = delta_{m,-j}: equals the Q-symbol at the antipode, <-n|A|-n> (below 1e-12)
   Uniform t is the average of the N + 1 vertices, the barycenter of the simplex, not a vertex. It keeps the trace
   and discards every direction; the vertex at m = j keeps the coherent-state value. Different maps.

T3. Strong zero preservation (every pure source) forces the vertex at m = j: the ray through Q.
   N = 12: all 12 states |j,m> with m != j are nodal at the pole, each forcing its own t_m = 0: yes
   N = 20: all 20 states |j,m> with m != j are nodal at the pole, each forcing its own t_m = 0: yes
   N = 30: all 30 states |j,m> with m != j are nodal at the pole, each forcing its own t_m = 0: yes
   Therefore t_m = 0 for every m != j, so E(z) is a nonnegative multiple of |j,j><j,j|: the ray through Q.
   Normalization (sum of t = 1) fixes the multiple at 1, which is Q itself.

T4. Weak zero preservation (the shell's own invariant only) does NOT force Q.
   N = 12: 12/12 vertices are nodal. The 5-fold stabilizer of a nodal direction allows only m = 0 mod 5
           (3 values: [5, 0, -5]); the invariant's support there is 3 of them: [5, 0, -5]
           5 half-turn axes perpendicular to the nodal axis also preserve it; each sends |j,0> to (-1)^j |j,0>,
           and j = 6 is even, so the m = 0 amplitude of the rotated invariant is free (here 0.6633).
           Weak preservation kills 3 of the 13 weights and leaves a 10-parameter cone; Q is one point in it.
           Explicit second member (uniform on the surviving m): vanishes at every nodal direction (below 1e-15),
           and at a non-nodal axis gives 0.086420 where Q gives 0.115226. Weak preservation does not tell them apart.
   N = 20: 20/20 face centres are nodal. The 3-fold stabilizer of a nodal direction allows only m = 0 mod 3
           (7 values: [9, 6, 3, 0, -3, -6, -9]); the invariant's support there is 7 of them: [9, 6, 3, 0, -3, -6, -9]
           3 half-turn axes perpendicular to the nodal axis also preserve it; each sends |j,0> to (-1)^j |j,0>,
           and j = 10 is even, so the m = 0 amplitude of the rotated invariant is free (here 0.5601).
           Weak preservation kills 7 of the 21 weights and leaves a 14-parameter cone; Q is one point in it.
           Explicit second member (uniform on the surviving m): vanishes at every nodal direction (below 1e-15),
           and at a non-nodal axis gives 0.062019 where Q gives 0.099733. Weak preservation does not tell them apart.
   N = 30: 30/30 edge midpoints are nodal. The 2-fold stabilizer of a nodal direction allows only m = 0 mod 2
           (15 values: [14, 12, 10, 8, 6, 4, 2, 0, -2, -4, -6, -8, -10, -12, -14]); the invariant's support there is 14 of them: [14, 12, 10, 8, 6, 4, 2, -2, -4, -6, -8, -10, -12, -14]
           2 half-turn axes perpendicular to the nodal axis also preserve it; each sends |j,0> to (-1)^j |j,0>,
           and j = 15 is odd, so the m = 0 amplitude of the rotated invariant is below 1e-12.
           Weak preservation kills 14 of the 31 weights and leaves a 17-parameter cone; Q is one point in it.
           Explicit second member (uniform on the surviving m): vanishes at every nodal direction (below 1e-15),
           and at a non-nodal axis gives 0.040809 where Q gives 0.080080. Weak preservation does not tell them apart.
   The gap between T3 and T4 is what MIT would have to supply. Preservation for the shell's own invariant can be
   formulated from the realized source alone; preservation for every pure state on the shell is a statement about
   the map; only the second gives Q.

T5. The nodal sets on the one-invariant shells, against step one's Majorana constellations.
   N = 12: zeros at 12/12 five-fold, 0/20 three-fold, 0/30 two-fold axes; 2j = 12 zeros expected on vertices; antipodally closed: True
           each zero is simple: at every nodal direction the rotated invariant's top component is m = 5 = j - 1.
   N = 20: zeros at 0/12 five-fold, 20/20 three-fold, 0/30 two-fold axes; 2j = 20 zeros expected on face centres; antipodally closed: True
           each zero is simple: at every nodal direction the rotated invariant's top component is m = 9 = j - 1.
   N = 30: zeros at 0/12 five-fold, 0/20 three-fold, 30/30 two-fold axes; 2j = 30 zeros expected on edge midpoints; antipodally closed: True
           each zero is simple: at every nodal direction the rotated invariant's top component is m = 14 = j - 1.
   The zero count matches 2j = N in each case, and each nodal set is antipodally closed, so the zero set of
   the overlap and the Majorana constellation agree as sets on these shells.

T6. What reaches the prediction. Below N = 60 the source is rank one, so a transfer meets it only through
    f_m(n) = |<j,m|D_n^dagger psi_N>|^2, and the predicted pattern is sum_m t_m f_m.
   N = 12: f_-m = f_m (below 1e-12); every f_m integrates to 4 pi/(N+1) (below 1e-12).
           Density multipoles of psi_N nonzero at ranks [0, 6, 10, 12] (4; smallest 0.28), zero at the other ranks (below 1e-12).
           Distinct even degrees <= 12 carrying an A5 invariant: [0, 6, 10, 12] (4; 4 harmonics with multiplicity).
           Diagonal transfers reach 13 of 13 ranks, Q's E(z) answers at 13, and the weight swap changes exactly the odd ranks (all 6 of them).
           Span over all m: rank 4 (smallest kept singular value 2.1, largest dropped below 1e-12);
           over the 10 weights weak preservation leaves: rank 3 (smallest kept 2.3, largest dropped below 1e-12).
           Weight moved from the vertex at -j to the vertex at j, t_{+-j} = (1 +- 1/2)/(N+1): on psi_N the pattern
           is P1's flat 1/(N+1) (below 1e-12); on the coherent source at the pole it is 0.115385 at the pole and 0.038462 at the antipode.
   N = 20: f_-m = f_m (below 1e-12); every f_m integrates to 4 pi/(N+1) (below 1e-12).
           Density multipoles of psi_N nonzero at ranks [0, 6, 10, 12, 16, 18, 20] (7; smallest 0.22), zero at the other ranks (below 1e-12).
           Distinct even degrees <= 20 carrying an A5 invariant: [0, 6, 10, 12, 16, 18, 20] (7; 7 harmonics with multiplicity).
           Diagonal transfers reach 21 of 21 ranks, Q's E(z) answers at 21, and the weight swap changes exactly the odd ranks (all 10 of them).
           Span over all m: rank 7 (smallest kept singular value 1.3, largest dropped below 1e-12);
           over the 14 weights weak preservation leaves: rank 6 (smallest kept 0.7, largest dropped below 1e-12).
           Weight moved from the vertex at -j to the vertex at j, t_{+-j} = (1 +- 1/2)/(N+1): on psi_N the pattern
           is P1's flat 1/(N+1) (below 1e-12); on the coherent source at the pole it is 0.071429 at the pole and 0.023810 at the antipode.
   N = 30: f_-m = f_m (below 1e-12); every f_m integrates to 4 pi/(N+1) (below 1e-12).
           Density multipoles of psi_N nonzero at ranks [0, 6, 10, 12, 16, 18, 20, 22, 24, 26, 28, 30] (12; smallest 0.07), zero at the other ranks (below 1e-12).
           Distinct even degrees <= 30 carrying an A5 invariant: [0, 6, 10, 12, 16, 18, 20, 22, 24, 26, 28, 30] (12; 13 harmonics with multiplicity).
           Diagonal transfers reach 31 of 31 ranks, Q's E(z) answers at 31, and the weight swap changes exactly the odd ranks (all 15 of them).
           Span over all m: rank 12 (smallest kept singular value 0.25, largest dropped below 1e-12);
           over the 17 weights weak preservation leaves: rank 9 (smallest kept 0.22, largest dropped below 1e-12).
           Weight moved from the vertex at -j to the vertex at j, t_{+-j} = (1 +- 1/2)/(N+1): on psi_N the pattern
           is P1's flat 1/(N+1) (below 1e-12); on the coherent source at the pole it is 0.048387 at the pole and 0.016129 at the antipode.
   After normalization, which is one condition since every f_m has the same integral:
   N = 12: the transfer keeps 12 free parameters,  9 under weak preservation; the predicted pattern keeps  3, 2 under it.
   N = 20: the transfer keeps 20 free parameters, 13 under weak preservation; the predicted pattern keeps  6, 5 under it.
   N = 30: the transfer keeps 30 free parameters, 16 under weak preservation; the predicted pattern keeps 11, 8 under it.
   N = 60, where the invariant is no longer unique:
           The invariants form a plane (dimension 2). A generic one is not fixed by time reversal (|<v|Theta v>| = 0.56):
           its pairing fails (max |f_m - f_-m| = 0.098) and its constellation is not centrally symmetric (max |Q(n) - Q(-n)| = 0.015).
           A time-reversal-fixed one pairs (below 1e-12), with an even Q-function (below 1e-12): below N = 60, uniqueness is what forces the pairing.
   Time reversal throughout is exp(-i pi J_y) then complex conjugation, Theta v_m = (-1)^(j-m) v_-m at N = 12, 20, 30 and 60
   (below 1e-12): the Surviving Ray's Theta_j with epsilon_j = 1.
   Most of the cone never reaches a rank-one source. The weak condition leaves the predicted pattern undetermined,
   by the amounts in the last column, and leaves the map undetermined by more.

T7. The real-field quotient. A real field's covariance commutes with time reversal, so only the pair sums
    u_0 = t_0 and u_m = t_m + t_-m act on it; what the weak family leaves open runs through a sign change.
   N = 12: on a random time-reversal-invariant covariance (invariance below 1e-12), two transfers with the same pair sums
           agree (below 1e-12); on a generic covariance they differ (above 1e-3); Q and the antipodal Q agree on it (below 1e-12).
           The j + 1 = 7 pair-sum vertices give independent patterns on it (rank 7). The time-reversal-fixed states
           |j,0> and (|j,m0> + e^{ia}|j,-m0>)/sqrt 2, 0 < m0 < j, are nodal at the pole: yes.
           Weak preservation kills the pair sums at |m| = [0, 5] and leaves 5 of 7.
           Leading anisotropic response (rank 6 over rank 0) across the weak family, as a ratio to Q's: from -0.909 (|m| = 1)
           to +1.955 (|m| = 3); the exhibited second member sits at +0.682.
   N = 20: on a random time-reversal-invariant covariance (invariance below 1e-12), two transfers with the same pair sums
           agree (below 1e-12); on a generic covariance they differ (above 1e-3); Q and the antipodal Q agree on it (below 1e-12).
           The j + 1 = 11 pair-sum vertices give independent patterns on it (rank 11). The time-reversal-fixed states
           |j,0> and (|j,m0> + e^{ia}|j,-m0>)/sqrt 2, 0 < m0 < j, are nodal at the pole: yes.
           Weak preservation kills the pair sums at |m| = [0, 3, 6, 9] and leaves 7 of 11.
           Leading anisotropic response (rank 6 over rank 0) across the weak family, as a ratio to Q's: from -0.989 (|m| = 8)
           to +1.000 (|m| = 10); the exhibited second member sits at +0.088.
   N = 30: on a random time-reversal-invariant covariance (invariance below 1e-12), two transfers with the same pair sums
           agree (below 1e-12); on a generic covariance they differ (above 1e-3); Q and the antipodal Q agree on it (below 1e-12).
           The j + 1 = 16 pair-sum vertices give independent patterns on it (rank 16). The time-reversal-fixed states
           |j,0> and (|j,m0> + e^{ia}|j,-m0>)/sqrt 2, 0 < m0 < j, are nodal at the pole: yes.
           Weak preservation kills the pair sums at |m| = [2, 4, 6, 8, 10, 12, 14] and leaves 9 of 16.
           Leading anisotropic response (rank 6 over rank 0) across the weak family, as a ratio to Q's: from -0.834 (|m| = 13)
           to +1.000 (|m| = 15); the exhibited second member sits at +0.022.
   After normalization the real-field map keeps 6, 10, 15 free parameters, and 4, 6, 8 under weak preservation.
